WEBVTT

02:05.325 --> 02:07.498
You look like you're doing all right.

02:09.896 --> 02:12.672
Father Time has his way with us all.

02:13.900 --> 02:15.902
Looks like you must have pissed him off.

02:24.244 --> 02:25.245
Ahem.

02:25.746 --> 02:27.123
Why we here?

02:29.016 --> 02:32.828
All right. You know that thing
the State PD is asking about,

02:32.919 --> 02:35.092
the Lake Charles murder.

02:36.156 --> 02:39.865
Shouldn't that have been in the papers
or online somewhere by now'?

02:41.128 --> 02:43.506
I mean, we can't trust them.

02:43.597 --> 02:45.770
I mean, if they go cover
something like that up,

02:45.832 --> 02:47.778
who knows what else they've covered up.

02:48.502 --> 02:49.947
What you think?

02:51.672 --> 02:56.121
I think you don't look particularly
healthy, listening to you talk.

02:56.510 --> 03:00.788
Your eyes, you seem kind of brittle, Rust.

03:01.615 --> 03:05.188
Most of the last decade
I spent stone drunk.

03:05.652 --> 03:08.064
Functional, but hammered.

03:08.989 --> 03:13.495
Went back to Alaska. Spent eight
years working fishing boats, bars.

03:13.660 --> 03:15.571
Oh, I thought you didn't like the cold.

03:15.662 --> 03:17.073
I hate it.

03:17.164 --> 03:20.407
And then I come back hereto Louisiana
for the first time in 2010.

03:20.500 --> 03:22.138
And why is that?

03:22.402 --> 03:25.815
The same reason I'm sitting
across the table from you now.

03:27.074 --> 03:29.213
A man remembers his debts.

03:31.645 --> 03:33.488
I don't dwell in the past.

03:34.347 --> 03:35.883
Well, it must be nice.

03:35.982 --> 03:39.191
I'm not interested in whatever
it is you think you owe me.

03:39.252 --> 03:40.856
Well, I don't owe you.

03:40.921 --> 03:44.027
We left something undone.

03:44.658 --> 03:46.535
We got to fix it.

03:46.593 --> 03:49.870
I've been working on this for two years.
Me. Myself.

03:49.930 --> 03:51.910
I never called you.
I never bothered you with it.

03:51.998 --> 03:53.238
Yeah, why would you?

03:53.333 --> 03:56.906
Shit, man! What, did you alienate
every other person in your life

03:57.003 --> 03:59.244
and then finally you came back
to me in the rotation?

03:59.339 --> 04:00.283
You know, not for nothing,

04:00.373 --> 04:02.375
but if you hadn't clipped Ledoux back then,

04:02.442 --> 04:04.888
we might have got the whole fucking story
out of him.

04:06.513 --> 04:10.051
You know, I think I'm going to
finish this beer and say so long.

04:10.117 --> 04:12.119
I'm not much of a drinker nowadays.

04:12.219 --> 04:15.200
In fact, I hadn't had a drop in three weeks
till I ran into you.

04:15.255 --> 04:17.257
I don't need you to drink, Marty.

04:17.357 --> 04:19.394
- I need you to help me.
- Why would I?

04:19.860 --> 04:21.897
They say you can't account for your time.

04:21.962 --> 04:26.104
They got eyewitnesses placing you
at the Lake Charles crime scene.

04:26.199 --> 04:28.975
You got some storage shed
that you won't let 'em look at.

04:29.069 --> 04:30.446
- That's right.
- Why not?

04:30.537 --> 04:33.040
Why not shoot straight with them?
You're innocent.

04:33.106 --> 04:34.779
Help them stop wasting their time.

04:34.875 --> 04:38.152
Fucking since when did guilt
and innocence define the State PD, huh'?

04:38.712 --> 04:40.316
Come the fuck on!

04:40.413 --> 04:42.333
I don't know the sprawl of this thing,
all right?

04:42.382 --> 04:46.558
The people I'm after, they're all fucking
over. They're in a lot of different things.

04:46.620 --> 04:48.622
Pieces. Family trees.

04:49.556 --> 04:53.129
The only way for you to understand
what I'm onto here is for me to show you.

04:53.226 --> 04:55.297
You got to come see what I got.

04:55.896 --> 04:57.466
No. You know what?

04:57.564 --> 05:00.272
I don't think I've been
very clear with you, Rust.

05:00.333 --> 05:04.076
If you were drowning,
I'd throw you a fucking barbell.

05:04.805 --> 05:07.809
Why would I ever help you?

05:14.014 --> 05:16.494
Because you have a debt.

05:26.259 --> 05:28.261
You got some fucking sack.

05:28.528 --> 05:31.168
What's that mean, I have a debt, huh?

05:31.264 --> 05:34.609
Means the way shit went down in '95,

05:34.668 --> 05:36.773
this is on you, too, buddy.

05:45.345 --> 05:47.484
What do you got to show me?

07:03.023 --> 07:04.559
What you packing?

07:08.228 --> 07:09.866
.38.

07:11.398 --> 07:12.741
Hollow-point?

07:13.099 --> 07:14.578
Yeah.

07:14.634 --> 07:16.204
That'll do it.

07:25.312 --> 07:27.724
You can never be too careful.

07:44.297 --> 07:48.074
All right, remember
there was no physical evidence

07:48.234 --> 07:52.148
connecting Dora Lange to
Ledoux's place out in the woods.

07:52.238 --> 07:56.653
Meaning it probably didn't happen out there.
Nobody was in a hurry to bring that up.

07:56.743 --> 08:00.418
Two. Women and children going missing.

08:00.480 --> 08:04.121
All taken from areas within
a 10-mile radius of schools

08:04.184 --> 08:06.994
that were funded by
Tuttle's Wellspring initiative.

08:07.087 --> 08:10.591
We establish a connection,
who's in, who's out, you know?

08:10.657 --> 08:14.264
I mean, do people disappear in equal
numbers in other parts of the state?

08:14.361 --> 08:17.171
- How many schools were there?
- Fourteen.

08:17.263 --> 08:19.504
Now, I've covered a surface area.

08:19.599 --> 08:22.705
I pulled runaways in state
and missing persons.

08:22.802 --> 08:26.443
Now, if you'll notice, there's twice as
many along the bayous. I don't know why.

08:26.506 --> 08:28.782
Hell, someone should do a study as to why.

08:29.442 --> 08:31.285
Now you're just throwing up stats.

08:31.344 --> 08:34.348
Why was Turtle so interested
in the Lange case, huh?

08:34.514 --> 08:37.688
Remember Charlie Lange
said what Ledoux told him?

08:37.784 --> 08:40.196
He said there's a group of men, sacrifices.

08:40.286 --> 08:42.789
Well, I think Turtle recognized the scene.

08:42.856 --> 08:45.860
That's why he came down there
jiminy quick with a fucking taskforce,

08:45.959 --> 08:48.337
and that's why he tripped out
when I talked to him in '02.

08:48.395 --> 08:50.204
Okay, so what happened to him?

08:50.997 --> 08:55.878
I mean, I'm looking around here
and I don't see or hear anything

08:55.969 --> 08:57.880
that doesn't make this all conjectural.

08:59.139 --> 09:01.085
1988.

09:01.207 --> 09:06.486
Accusations of child molestation
at a preschool funded by Tuttle.

09:06.546 --> 09:09.152
The name of that school
was Shepherd's Flock.

09:09.249 --> 09:12.719
It shuts down, reopens two years
later on Pelican Island

09:12.819 --> 09:17.325
under the name Light of the Way Academy,
where Rianne Olivier went.

09:17.390 --> 09:20.564
Now, I got an enrollment list.
Sixteen kids in the class.

09:20.660 --> 09:22.367
One of them turned out to be a young man

09:22.429 --> 09:25.239
who just showed up
for solicitation in New Orleans.

09:31.004 --> 09:35.578
Now this is 2010.
His name is Toby Boelert.

09:35.942 --> 09:38.081
Goes by the name of Johnny Joanie.

09:47.353 --> 09:49.196
Shepherd's Flock.

09:50.523 --> 09:53.265
Why are you asking me about that place?

09:53.359 --> 09:57.466
After that place shut down,
there was a lot of talk going around...

09:58.765 --> 10:00.540
You ever see that reverend,

10:01.468 --> 10:03.038
Billy Lee Tuttle, around?

10:03.103 --> 10:06.482
You know, I think so.
But who can remember way back?

10:07.107 --> 10:08.814
That's how it all started.

10:09.309 --> 10:11.550
Memory be fucked.

10:12.645 --> 10:16.650
I decided it all had to be a dream anyways.
And I don't remember if...

10:20.053 --> 10:21.430
We'd go to sleep.

10:22.889 --> 10:26.132
Only sometimes I didn't feel like I was
asleep. I felt like I was still awake.

10:26.226 --> 10:29.139
But I must have been asleep
because I couldn't move.

10:29.662 --> 10:33.576
Just sort of see under my eyelids.

10:34.501 --> 10:35.980
Then what?

10:36.769 --> 10:38.476
I don't know.

10:38.571 --> 10:40.073
There were men,

10:41.574 --> 10:43.611
taking pictures.

10:44.410 --> 10:48.017
Sometimes other things.

10:48.615 --> 10:51.755
- Who were they?
- I don't know.

10:51.818 --> 10:54.094
They had animal faces.

10:54.154 --> 10:56.930
That's why I decided it had to be a dream.

10:56.990 --> 11:00.267
They had animal faces.
Well, it had to be a dream.

11:00.326 --> 11:02.636
Any other kids see this?

11:02.695 --> 11:03.696
One girl.

11:05.031 --> 11:09.173
I don't remember her name.
She first started talking about it.

11:09.269 --> 11:11.647
She seen it, too, the faces.

11:11.704 --> 11:15.015
- I do not remember her name.
- Marie Fontenot.

11:17.110 --> 11:18.316
Maybe.

11:19.279 --> 11:21.384
You ever see any of these men's faces?

11:21.481 --> 11:24.724
Once. They didn't all have animal faces.

11:26.953 --> 11:31.163
Three younger men. I don't remember them.
Just one.

11:31.824 --> 11:34.202
He had bad scars all around his mouth.

11:34.294 --> 11:37.207
Like the bottom half got all burned up.

11:39.165 --> 11:41.042
And you know what?

11:41.134 --> 11:44.013
I thought that meant it was a dream, too.

11:47.006 --> 11:49.885
No, I don't think it was a dream.

11:51.044 --> 11:52.084
HART". I don't understand.

11:52.178 --> 11:56.388
Are you saying that you think
that this hypothetical killer

11:56.482 --> 11:59.156
was, uh, an old school teacher?

11:59.219 --> 12:02.689
Or it might, what, involve State PD?

12:02.755 --> 12:05.395
Goddamn, what happened to you, man?

12:06.426 --> 12:08.872
You remember him? Hmm?

12:09.696 --> 12:11.437
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

12:11.531 --> 12:13.738
You and I are on the case in Erath.

12:13.833 --> 12:16.439
A girl comes forward and says
she was chased through the woods

12:16.536 --> 12:18.675
by a spaghetti monster with green ears.

12:18.738 --> 12:23.710
Now I think that this is our man
with the scars on his face.

12:23.776 --> 12:25.449
I've got three references.

12:25.545 --> 12:30.051
Seventeen years ago, that old revival church
said a tall man with scars came through.

12:30.116 --> 12:35.122
Kelly Reider, in the hospital. And, now,
this hooker from the Quarter, Toby.

12:35.221 --> 12:36.928
I don't know who he is.
I don't know where he is.

12:37.023 --> 12:40.732
I don't know where this thing fucking
starts, but it ends with him.

12:42.262 --> 12:44.868
All right, you know that little township
down around Erath?

12:44.931 --> 12:48.105
All right?
That's where the Turtle family is from.

12:48.201 --> 12:50.875
Now, it used to be a pirate hideout.

12:50.970 --> 12:53.473
Now they turned it
into plantations or whatnot.

12:53.573 --> 12:56.144
Had a very rural sense of Mardi Gras.

12:57.310 --> 13:00.052
Uh, you know, the men on horses,
animal masks, and such.

13:00.113 --> 13:02.821
- Courir de Mardi Gras.
- That's right.

13:02.915 --> 13:07.125
Now, they had an annual winter festival,
all right, heavy on the Saturnalia.

13:07.220 --> 13:10.793
A place where that Santeria
and Voudon all mashed together.

13:10.890 --> 13:11.891
Have a look.

13:11.958 --> 13:13.904
From the winter festival.

13:15.261 --> 13:16.569
Blindfold.

13:17.430 --> 13:19.432
Antlers. Mask.

13:21.467 --> 13:26.610
I got these from a series an artist
did in Kenner, right after Katrina.

13:26.673 --> 13:31.281
Says he kept running across these
"stick things" as he called them.

13:31.344 --> 13:32.846
Look familiar?

13:34.080 --> 13:37.118
I think our man had a real good time
after the hurricane.

13:37.617 --> 13:40.860
Chaos. People missing. People gone.

13:40.953 --> 13:42.296
Cops gone.

13:43.289 --> 13:45.428
I think he had a real good year.

13:45.992 --> 13:47.938
What do you need me for'?

13:48.961 --> 13:53.933
You got friends on the force.
You have access that I don't. Databases.

13:54.100 --> 13:57.604
I need case files. I need missing persons.
I need homicides.

13:57.670 --> 14:00.344
I need title transfers, auto and home.

14:00.440 --> 14:03.182
I got a list of names. I'm gonna need
background checks, tax records.

14:03.276 --> 14:04.983
Anything we can get on Ledoux.

14:05.044 --> 14:06.387
Jesus Christ, man.

14:06.479 --> 14:09.358
I wouldn't have called you
and I wouldn't have fucking bothered you

14:09.449 --> 14:12.055
if State wouldn't have pulled me in
on this Lake Charles case.

14:12.151 --> 14:13.653
Well, if you need help,

14:13.720 --> 14:16.462
why don't you just give it
to Papania and Gilbough?

14:16.522 --> 14:19.082
No, they may be pawns in this thing
and not even fucking know it.

14:19.158 --> 14:20.660
- Come on.
- Look, Eddie Tuttle

14:20.727 --> 14:22.866
is the goddamn senator of this state.

14:22.962 --> 14:25.738
The late Reverend Billy Lee Turtle
is his cousin.

14:25.832 --> 14:27.812
I'm telling you, it's a
fucking family thing.

14:27.867 --> 14:30.370
That's what I mean
when I talk about the sprawl, Marty.

14:30.470 --> 14:33.576
Eddie Tuttle is the reason that
the Lake Charles thing never made the wire.

14:33.673 --> 14:36.381
Look, man' you have
some compelling stuff here.

14:36.476 --> 14:38.319
And you might have something.

14:41.247 --> 14:46.856
But all this "sprawl," as you call it,
which I would call "conjecture,"

14:46.986 --> 14:49.592
this shit about the
Tuttles and the State PD,

14:49.689 --> 14:53.569
do you know how fucking crazy that sounds?

14:53.659 --> 14:55.935
It's like you've been alone too long.

14:56.028 --> 15:02.240
Like you, maybe, told yourself this story
and kept drinking until you believed it.

15:02.335 --> 15:03.575
Marty.

15:07.173 --> 15:10.848
I had my time where I wondered
if this was all in my head.

15:12.545 --> 15:14.218
That time passed.

15:15.181 --> 15:16.524
Really?

15:21.521 --> 15:24.400
What happened to Billy Lee Tuttle?

15:27.760 --> 15:30.707
There's something
you're going to have to look at.

15:31.864 --> 15:33.207
No other way around it.

15:38.304 --> 15:39.944
You still take your coffee black?

15:40.706 --> 15:42.947
Oh, uh, green tea,
if you have it.

15:43.042 --> 15:45.784
I've been trying to stay away
from coffee, you know,

15:45.878 --> 15:47.653
a little bit healthier.

15:47.747 --> 15:51.388
So, Mace, is she, uh,
back from Chicago yet?

15:51.584 --> 15:54.724
- Mmm-hmm, three months ago.
- Three months?

15:55.087 --> 15:56.088
Uh...

15:57.256 --> 15:59.793
- What was that? That...
- AmeriCorps.

16:00.560 --> 16:02.597
- Oh.
Leaching.

16:02.662 --> 16:04.573
And Audrey, how is she?

16:04.630 --> 16:07.133
She's fine at the moment.

16:07.233 --> 16:10.578
She sometimes decides
she doesn't need her meds.

16:11.404 --> 16:14.578
I like her boyfriend.
He watches out for her.

16:14.640 --> 16:17.484
She had an art show in New Orleans.

16:17.577 --> 16:18.954
Sold some paintings.

16:19.011 --> 16:24.791
Well, that's good. That's great. I should
buy one, I mean, if I can afford it.

16:29.856 --> 16:32.302
So the reason I, uh...

16:32.358 --> 16:35.305
I mean, like I said on the phone,

16:35.361 --> 16:37.602
I want to ask you about those cops.

16:38.931 --> 16:41.468
They just wanted to know
about you and Rust.

16:41.601 --> 16:42.944
Mostly Rust.

16:43.002 --> 16:47.144
They wanted to know about the fight in '02.

16:51.010 --> 16:53.684
- Mmm' did you tell them?
- No.

16:54.947 --> 16:57.120
But they think Rust did something.

16:58.284 --> 17:00.662
I know. He didn't.

17:00.786 --> 17:02.697
I didn't think he did.

17:08.027 --> 17:10.633
You talk to him?

17:13.399 --> 17:15.345
No. Not since.

17:16.636 --> 17:17.637
You?

17:18.404 --> 17:22.011
Yeah. I mean, after they brought me in.
Yeah.

17:23.409 --> 17:26.253
- How is he?
Different. Same.

17:26.345 --> 17:29.849
I mean, he's lived rough
for a long time now.

17:32.018 --> 17:34.225
He always did, it seemed like.

17:34.987 --> 17:36.523
Taken a toll.

17:39.258 --> 17:41.101
He needs my help.

17:42.094 --> 17:43.767
Are you going to help him?

17:47.567 --> 17:48.739
Yes.

17:49.602 --> 17:50.672
Why?

17:52.505 --> 17:53.677
I have to.

17:54.674 --> 17:57.052
What is it?
What do the police think he did?

17:57.109 --> 17:59.715
I cant talk about that. It's P.l. stuff.

17:59.779 --> 18:03.249
He's hiring the firm. I'm hiring him.

18:03.349 --> 18:04.419
All this time,

18:04.517 --> 18:06.360
you two, and just...

18:07.019 --> 18:08.362
Just like that?

18:10.690 --> 18:12.431
Oh, I took some convincing.

18:15.461 --> 18:17.634
COHLE". I looked in Billys eyes.

18:17.964 --> 18:19.534
He looked in mine.

18:20.199 --> 18:21.701
He got me suspended.

18:24.070 --> 18:27.779
Now, Billy Lee Tuttle
owns three houses in Louisiana.

18:27.873 --> 18:31.286
One in Shreveport, one in Baton Rouge,
one in New Orleans.

18:31.377 --> 18:33.983
Also one in Florida.

18:34.080 --> 18:37.823
I waited till he went on his
Spring Ministry Tour in 2010.

18:37.917 --> 18:40.420
Look, Rust, I changed my mind.

18:40.486 --> 18:43.467
If you did something,
I don't want to hear about it.

18:43.556 --> 18:46.400
Remember I told you
about my stint in robbery?

18:46.993 --> 18:49.234
I make a pretty ace B&E man.

18:51.230 --> 18:54.006
Now,
I staked his places out for weeks.

18:54.100 --> 18:57.638
Checked surveillance.
Mapped security. I found ingresses.

18:57.737 --> 18:59.648
And here I am, you know,

18:59.739 --> 19:02.686
my whole life is this
one expanding, circular fuck-up

19:02.775 --> 19:04.175
and I think it's about to close out

19:04.243 --> 19:06.689
with me getting clipped in a home invasion.

19:06.779 --> 19:08.417
All right, what I'm saying is

19:08.481 --> 19:11.621
I was aware that I might have lost my mind.

19:23.462 --> 19:25.669
But after the second home,

19:27.366 --> 19:30.313
doubt got taken behind the woodshed
and put down.

19:33.873 --> 19:37.685
You'll notice he never reported
the Baton Rouge break-in.

19:37.777 --> 19:40.018
Just the Shreveport house.

19:40.112 --> 19:42.786
I found those in the safe there.

19:42.848 --> 19:45.954
The paper stock's over 15 years old.

19:46.018 --> 19:49.022
- God damn it.
- These...

19:49.121 --> 19:52.625
They aren't as bad if you don't
know what you're looking at.

19:57.229 --> 19:58.572
Motherfuck!

20:05.905 --> 20:06.975
And

20:10.409 --> 20:12.514
there was a videotape.

20:28.327 --> 20:30.238
Take a look.

21:42.802 --> 21:43.837
No!

21:45.471 --> 21:46.779
God!

21:48.174 --> 21:49.414
Jesus!

21:49.475 --> 21:50.647
Ohh!

21:52.745 --> 21:53.849
Fuck!

22:00.085 --> 22:01.189
Fuck!

22:04.423 --> 22:05.925
You watch all of that?

22:06.759 --> 22:07.760
Yeah.

22:09.195 --> 22:12.176
I had to see if any of the men
took off their mask.

22:12.264 --> 22:13.800
None did.

22:15.034 --> 22:16.377
Oh, fuck!

22:17.503 --> 22:21.280
I won't avert my eyes. Not again.

22:23.275 --> 22:24.777
Jesus Christ.

22:28.814 --> 22:31.055
That little girl's Marie Fontenot.

22:35.287 --> 22:37.358
Did you kill Tuttle?

22:37.456 --> 22:38.456
No.

22:38.490 --> 22:43.337
I assumed that he was thinking
he was going to be blackmailed.

22:43.395 --> 22:46.569
And I think some people
took him out after they found out

22:46.665 --> 22:49.669
what was taken from the safe,
before he had a chance to.

22:51.737 --> 22:55.014
What can I do to help?

22:57.409 --> 23:00.856
We start by pulling everything
there is on Dora Lange.

23:01.981 --> 23:05.895
And I got names, I got family members,
Tuttle connections.

23:05.985 --> 23:11.264
Any information that we can get
on Reggie or Dewall Ledoux.

23:11.357 --> 23:15.567
All right, we can coordinate
out of your offices if you want.

23:23.269 --> 23:24.748
You shouldn't have that.

23:29.341 --> 23:31.184
Nobody should have this.

23:39.451 --> 23:43.194
I'm glad that you're doing good,
Maggie.

23:44.256 --> 23:46.862
It seems like everybody is happy,
and it's...

23:48.093 --> 23:50.039
Ahem. It's good to see.

23:51.397 --> 23:55.368
Thank you for everything.

23:57.303 --> 24:00.216
I haven! seen you in over two years' Marty.

24:03.409 --> 24:05.980
Did you come hereto say goodbye?

24:09.248 --> 24:12.718
Thank you, Maggie. I mean that.

24:40.846 --> 24:45.192
There's not gonna be a bunch of people
coming in and out of this place, is there?

24:45.284 --> 24:47.491
What do you think, Rust?

24:50.856 --> 24:54.303
Practical terms,
we're doing an identify and locate.

24:54.360 --> 24:58.706
Now, I can't afford to subscribe
to all the databases that I used to,

24:58.797 --> 25:03.610
but I got the AutoTrackXP
for motor vehicle records.

25:03.669 --> 25:09.210
I got FlatRate Info for
the Ql National People Locator.

25:09.308 --> 25:11.379
Public records, of course.

25:11.477 --> 25:13.650
All right, that sounds good.

25:20.686 --> 25:22.359
How you been? Ahem.

25:22.454 --> 25:25.128
You know, besides work, what do you do?

25:27.793 --> 25:28.999
Sorry. I just...

25:29.061 --> 25:32.406
I don't ever remember you askin' me
a personal question before.

25:33.799 --> 25:38.714
Uh, you know, I just stay busy, uh...

25:39.204 --> 25:41.707
Fish, girlfriends.

25:41.807 --> 25:43.548
You seem' anyway'?

25:44.476 --> 25:47.548
Not really. Some dates.

25:47.646 --> 25:49.887
You know, it's all pretty casual.

25:52.251 --> 25:55.926
I did have somethin' goin'
for a while, this Filipino girl.

25:56.021 --> 25:57.864
But that didn't pan out.

26:02.828 --> 26:06.037
Quiet life. I don't stay out late.
I just... I go home.

26:21.080 --> 26:23.526
- You?
- Yeah, I'm about the same.

26:24.616 --> 26:27.597
No girlfriend, just go to work and go home.

26:50.943 --> 26:54.823
How about that girl you were seeing
in '02'? What ever happened with her?

26:54.913 --> 26:59.953
Yeah, that was never going to last.
It never should have started.

27:00.052 --> 27:02.123
Yeah. No way.

27:02.221 --> 27:04.792
She, uh, had problems.

27:04.890 --> 27:06.961
You always liked 'em crazy.

27:07.960 --> 27:09.633
Yeah. That I did.

27:09.728 --> 27:11.674
Why did you quit, Marty?

27:13.398 --> 27:16.140
You could've been boss, you know.

27:16.235 --> 27:18.738
LT, at least. Captain.

27:19.771 --> 27:22.615
I did another four years after you left.

27:22.674 --> 27:26.520
And I guess the job just kind of
ran its course with me.

27:27.246 --> 27:29.089
How's that?

27:29.148 --> 27:32.857
I was gonna play baseball, ride bulls.

27:32.951 --> 27:36.660
You know, you end up becomin'
somethin' you never intended.

27:37.923 --> 27:41.496
Uh, I guess you never really even know why.

27:44.363 --> 27:47.173
I suppose I could've been a painter.

27:47.266 --> 27:51.180
You know, a historian.
Old scenes, new details.

27:52.137 --> 27:55.016
Yeah? Yeah, you do much paintin'?

27:55.107 --> 27:58.987
No. Little late in the game to
start somethin' like that, I reckon.

27:59.111 --> 28:02.649
Life's barely long enough
to get good at one thing.

28:03.682 --> 28:05.161
If that long.

28:05.217 --> 28:07.959
Yeah. So be careful what you get good at.

28:14.226 --> 28:16.866
What do you call a black man
who flies a plane?

28:16.962 --> 28:18.635
I don't know.

28:18.697 --> 28:21.974
A pilot, you racist bastard.
What else would you call him?

28:24.236 --> 28:27.581
Speaking of, you know I've been
takin' some writing courses.

28:27.673 --> 28:30.813
And, uh... No, I have.

28:30.909 --> 28:35.517
And, uh, I've been tinkerin' around
with this thing off and on.

28:35.581 --> 28:37.151
True crime.

28:37.216 --> 28:38.889
And that's the genre, not the title.

28:38.984 --> 28:41.055
- You serious?
- Yeah.

28:41.153 --> 28:44.498
You know' what happened in '95,
and some other old cases.

28:44.556 --> 28:50.563
And all I need from you, Bobby,
is some old copies of case files.

28:53.565 --> 28:56.409
You still like your single mall, don't you?

28:58.537 --> 29:01.177
Ah, I guess I do.

29:03.108 --> 29:06.214
What, business gotten so bad,
you got to become a writer?

29:06.278 --> 29:09.225
Nope. I've always wanted to do it.
I just never had the time.

29:09.281 --> 29:13.093
And in regards of files,
I'd like to avoid Fuck and Suck,

29:13.185 --> 29:15.256
the two dicks I spent last Saturday with.

29:15.354 --> 29:16.389
Hmm.

29:16.788 --> 29:19.462
Papania and Gilbough.
I hear you.

29:20.859 --> 29:22.270
Of course, man, whatever you need.

29:22.394 --> 29:24.396
Ah!

29:25.197 --> 29:27.609
Appreciate it, Bobby.
- No problem.

29:29.201 --> 29:33.308
Missing persons mostly,
maybe far back as the '80s.

29:33.405 --> 29:37.751
Well, anything before '05 that never became
part of an official investigation,

29:37.809 --> 29:39.948
it isn't gonna be in the computers.

29:40.045 --> 29:42.150
You're gonna have to
sort through the files.

29:53.325 --> 29:54.668
Thank you.

30:24.823 --> 30:26.530
Found somethin'. Background.

30:26.658 --> 30:30.196
Dewall Ledoux transferred title
on a truck to a Jimmy Ledoux.

30:30.295 --> 30:32.673
Appears like that might be a cousin.

30:32.764 --> 30:37.110
I found him in White Castle.
Owns an auto shop.

30:38.370 --> 30:40.281
All right.

30:40.339 --> 30:42.444
Did you pull that Marie Fontenot file?

30:43.608 --> 30:48.182
There wasn't one.
Report's gone. Back-trackin' that.

30:55.120 --> 30:58.727
Marty, this is Robert Doumain.
He owns the place.

30:59.825 --> 31:02.135
Hey, hows it goin'? Nice spot.

31:04.396 --> 31:06.706
He's not a cop no more, Robert.

31:07.632 --> 31:09.908
You got somethin' against cops?

31:10.836 --> 31:14.579
Bob had a little boy.
Been missin' since '85.

31:18.710 --> 31:20.053
Sorry.

31:21.646 --> 31:26.994
Jimmy Ledoux came up spotless.
Three kids, wife's a teacher.

31:27.052 --> 31:29.658
He coaches his boys peewee football team.

31:32.891 --> 31:34.234
Any relation?

31:34.326 --> 31:37.102
So many Ledouxs around,
I never had to worry about a connection.

31:37.195 --> 31:40.074
But, yeah, my dad's second cousin
or somethin'.

31:40.165 --> 31:42.441
My pop didn't like them none.

31:42.534 --> 31:46.107
Said they weren't white enough
to be white trash.

31:46.204 --> 31:48.081
What's this about exactly?

31:48.173 --> 31:50.585
Man asked us to locate his daughter.

31:50.675 --> 31:53.781
It was a long time ago, but it looks like
she might have known Dewall.

31:53.879 --> 31:54.919
Sorry 10 hear that.

31:55.013 --> 31:58.256
Must know what happened to them.
Sick shits.

31:59.951 --> 32:01.862
Pop said they died too quick.

32:01.920 --> 32:05.629
Is there anything you remember
that you can tell us about these guys?

32:05.724 --> 32:08.466
Just they were nuts. Looked at you funky.

32:09.628 --> 32:12.472
Reggie was always asking
about the girls in my school,

32:12.564 --> 32:15.773
and couple of times I saw him,
Dewall just said kooky stuff.

32:17.102 --> 32:19.981
Any chance you ever saw
a third man with them'?

32:20.071 --> 32:24.213
A man who had a bunch of scars
on the bottom of his face?

32:29.080 --> 32:31.720
It's weird you say that.

32:31.783 --> 32:33.592
I remember that face.

32:35.120 --> 32:37.930
My pop let 'em use our deer camp once,
took me with 'em.

32:37.989 --> 32:41.630
I was, like, 11.
They were, maybe, 10 years older than me.

32:41.726 --> 32:43.967
They introduced us. The guy,

32:45.063 --> 32:48.237
his face, underneath his nose
and cheeks, scarred.

32:49.801 --> 32:52.008
Gave me funny looks all night.

32:52.103 --> 32:54.583
Every time I glanced at him, starin' at me.

32:56.775 --> 32:59.779
Any chance this man with scars
was another Ledoux?

32:59.845 --> 33:02.951
No. I don't know. I don't think so.

33:04.449 --> 33:08.659
Next mornin', the men were too hungover
to hunt. Pop and I went home.

33:08.753 --> 33:12.098
You, uh, ever see him again,
the guy with the scars?

33:13.792 --> 33:15.829
Never again.

33:15.927 --> 33:17.429
I'd remember.

33:31.710 --> 33:34.054
Fuck, I don't like this place.

33:35.280 --> 33:37.783
Nothin' grows in the right direction.

33:39.951 --> 33:42.124
Where'd this woman come from?

33:43.355 --> 33:47.326
Tax records.
Drew a paycheck from Tuttle's father.

33:48.860 --> 33:50.737
Uh, some kind of domestic.

33:52.964 --> 33:53.965
How'd you find her?

33:54.799 --> 33:59.475
Well, I had to get federal income
tax records from '40 to '59.

34:00.872 --> 34:05.082
Match social with credit check run
in the late '90s

34:05.176 --> 34:08.020
for Section 8 housing in Alexandria.

34:09.180 --> 34:11.683
Mmm, good job. Look at you.

34:11.750 --> 34:12.888
- Heh!
- Hmm.

34:13.318 --> 34:15.525
High praise from a bartender.

34:31.336 --> 34:35.341
She gets tired easy,
especially hot as it is.

34:35.407 --> 34:37.409
I don't understand what this is about.

34:37.509 --> 34:39.420
Thank you.

34:39.511 --> 34:44.756
We're private investigators
hired to do, uh, ancestral research,

34:44.849 --> 34:47.022
mineral rights along the coast.

34:47.185 --> 34:48.255
Hmm.

34:49.087 --> 34:52.068
I never knew them Turtle people,
but I heard stories'

34:52.123 --> 34:54.399
No, thank you.

34:54.459 --> 34:56.302
You think she might get some money
out this?

34:56.394 --> 35:00.365
Uh, quite possible.
Depends on what we find out.

35:04.569 --> 35:06.048
Miss Dolores.

35:07.439 --> 35:11.444
You worked for Mr. Sam Turtle
19 years, right?

35:11.543 --> 35:13.887
Yes. Erath.

35:14.546 --> 35:15.786
Mmm-hmm.

35:16.748 --> 35:18.318
Then Shreveport.

35:18.416 --> 35:21.124
So you knew his son, Billy Lee?

35:21.219 --> 35:22.596
Right?
- Mmm-hmm.

35:22.654 --> 35:25.828
- A cousin, Eddie?
- Little boys. Mmm-hmm.

35:26.324 --> 35:29.100
- I remember 'em.
- What about extended family?

35:29.160 --> 35:32.232
Cousins, you know,
might have been close to the boys?

35:33.064 --> 35:35.408
Those days, families were bigger.

35:36.234 --> 35:40.910
Oh, all sorts of brothers, cousins,
kids just running around.

35:40.972 --> 35:45.580
Did, uh, Sam Tuttle have kids
outside his marriage that you know about?

35:45.644 --> 35:48.022
Hmm! Don't you know it.

35:50.148 --> 35:53.493
Now, people kept their own back then.

35:53.585 --> 35:57.260
I mean, a mans house was his own.

35:58.023 --> 36:02.267
Mr. Sam, he had lots of children,

36:02.327 --> 36:04.170
all types.

36:05.764 --> 36:07.641
He didn't like a woman...

36:11.269 --> 36:14.113
See, once she had it done to her,

36:14.773 --> 36:17.845
he didn't like 'em but that one time.

36:17.942 --> 36:19.888
- Not after that.
- Hmm.

36:20.345 --> 36:22.382
With all these kids runnin' around,

36:23.982 --> 36:28.727
you remember one that maybe had
scars all across the bottom of his face?

36:29.554 --> 36:33.366
Uh, I think that was Mr. Sam's grandchild.

36:33.458 --> 36:37.065
His daddy did that to him, that poor boy.

36:37.996 --> 36:41.534
I think that child was a Childress.

36:41.633 --> 36:44.239
What, FI? He was a LeBeau or a Childress?

36:44.335 --> 36:46.576
From Mr. Sam's other family?

36:49.407 --> 36:52.854
I shouldn't be talking to you about this.

36:52.911 --> 36:54.413
No, it's okay.

36:55.980 --> 36:57.482
Miss Dolores,

36:58.750 --> 37:00.830
could you have a look at somethin' for me?
One thing.

37:00.885 --> 37:03.695
Just have a look. See if you recognize it.

37:13.331 --> 37:14.935
You know Carcosa?

37:16.334 --> 37:17.335
What is it?

37:22.941 --> 37:25.945
Him who eats time.

37:29.080 --> 37:30.525
Him robes...

37:32.117 --> 37:35.291
It's a wind of invisible voices.

37:36.054 --> 37:37.465
"Mineral rights," my ass.

37:37.555 --> 37:39.228
- What y'all doin'?
- Rejoice.

37:40.358 --> 37:42.770
Death is not the end. Rejoice!

37:42.861 --> 37:44.061
You need to leave, now.

37:44.062 --> 37:45.973
Death is not the end.

37:46.064 --> 37:47.372
You need to leave.

37:47.432 --> 37:49.434
You know Carcosa.

37:50.568 --> 37:53.640
You rejoice. Carcosa...

38:22.400 --> 38:25.574
The rest of the family,
they don't really talk to Aunt D.

38:25.637 --> 38:28.413
She crazy. Dementia.

38:29.340 --> 38:32.651
She never had any kind of good life.
But most clays, she can't even make sense.

38:32.744 --> 38:34.815
Yeah? She sure made sense to me.

38:36.014 --> 38:38.255
That should worry you, mister.

38:49.093 --> 38:51.004
I sure hope that old lady was wrong.

38:51.696 --> 38:55.337
- About what?
- About death not being the end of it.

39:04.042 --> 39:07.114
Did some back-trackin'
on the Marie Fontenot stuff.

39:07.178 --> 39:08.486
Got some old sheets.

39:08.546 --> 39:12.016
Sheriff signed off on the
report made in error.

39:12.116 --> 39:15.029
But he didn't take
the original complaint on her.

39:15.119 --> 39:16.462
Deputy did.

39:18.323 --> 39:19.700
Got a name?

39:20.892 --> 39:22.803
You ain't going to believe this shit.

39:23.561 --> 39:25.507
Steve Geraci.

39:25.563 --> 39:27.474
So I did some double-checkin'.

39:27.532 --> 39:31.241
Before CID, he was with
Vermilion Parish Sheriffs.

39:31.336 --> 39:33.816
Erath was his beat.

39:33.872 --> 39:37.684
If it got covered up,
Steve might know something.

39:37.742 --> 39:41.656
Didn't say a fucking word
when we asked about it in '95.

39:41.713 --> 39:44.057
Oh, I never did like that cocksucker.

39:45.049 --> 39:46.357
Where is he now?

39:46.417 --> 39:48.829
Well, uh, this is the thing.

39:50.588 --> 39:55.731
He's from Iberia, originally.
After CID, he went home.

39:55.827 --> 39:58.865
He's sheriff of Iberia Parish.

39:58.930 --> 40:01.240
- Shit.
- Yeah.

40:01.332 --> 40:06.179
Rust, the only person can arrest
a sheriff in this state is the governor.

40:06.237 --> 40:09.275
Well, we ain't lookin'
to arrest him' Marty.

40:09.374 --> 40:11.547
Just have a little chat.

40:11.609 --> 40:13.555
He ain't gonna talk with you.

40:13.611 --> 40:17.058
I got a car battery and two jumper cables
who argue different.

40:17.115 --> 40:18.890
Don't even start with that shit.

40:18.950 --> 40:20.952
What do you recommend' Marty?

40:21.052 --> 40:24.590
Well, fuck, why don't you talk to him?
You two always liked each other.

40:25.456 --> 40:27.697
Well, what can I say? I'm a people person.

40:27.759 --> 40:29.705
Start with that, then.

40:34.532 --> 40:37.479
- Oh.
- Oh, come on.

40:37.568 --> 40:39.980
Just try to relax. Take your time.

40:43.441 --> 40:44.784
There you go.

40:44.876 --> 40:46.878
- Okay.
- Nice shot.

40:46.945 --> 40:48.891
What was that? Fifteen on the green?

40:49.080 --> 40:52.061
I don't know.

40:56.220 --> 40:59.724
Hey, you know, on the phone, you were
saying somethin' about that Fontenot girl.

40:59.791 --> 41:02.237
- Yeah.
- Why is that on your radar?

41:02.627 --> 41:05.608
Oh, it's nothing. It's just, uh...

41:05.663 --> 41:08.439
Extended family wants a locate.

41:09.600 --> 41:12.479
I didn't remember at the time, back in '95.

41:13.271 --> 41:16.480
- I was hit-tin' the bottle a lot back then.
- Yeah. Who wasn't?

41:17.842 --> 41:19.947
Twenty years ago, you know.

41:21.813 --> 41:24.919
My recall, girl's mom was single.

41:26.084 --> 41:27.529
Drug charges.

41:28.786 --> 41:29.787
Uh...

41:32.357 --> 41:35.167
Little girl went to live
with her birth daddy.

41:36.094 --> 41:39.268
I think. That is, if I'm rememberin' right.

41:40.431 --> 41:41.432
Uh...

41:41.499 --> 41:46.107
Momma didn't make a fuss after
the first notice, so she was fine with it.

41:49.273 --> 41:53.119
You talk to the family directly, back then?

41:53.177 --> 41:57.182
No. Ted Childress, the sheriff.
He knew 'em.

41:58.816 --> 42:00.159
Childress.

42:01.619 --> 42:03.292
Now, watch this.

42:05.890 --> 42:07.062
Whew!

42:07.892 --> 42:09.701
You like that?

42:09.794 --> 42:12.570
Seized it off a good ol' boy,
had a quarter bag of weed.

42:14.065 --> 42:16.705
Ooh. You got to love this country.

42:16.801 --> 42:19.805
- Good to see you again, man.
- Good to see you.

42:22.373 --> 42:27.015
Hey, uh, that client you got,
askin' about the Fontenot girl.

42:28.646 --> 42:31.149
You let 'em know I'd be
happy to talk to 'em.

42:31.215 --> 42:36.062
Oh, yeah. Distant relatives, Saint Louis,
trying to settle a tiny inheritance.

42:36.154 --> 42:37.997
Don't worry about it.

42:39.023 --> 42:43.062
Okay, well, they want to talk,
you let 'em know.

42:43.161 --> 42:44.162
Yeah.

42:44.228 --> 42:46.435
Don't go too fast, Sheriff.

42:46.531 --> 42:48.408
Not me.

42:48.499 --> 42:51.776
- Let's do it again sometime.
- Yeah, I'd like that.

43:01.946 --> 43:03.016
Hey.

43:04.415 --> 43:07.089
Better get those jumper cables ready.

43:07.185 --> 43:09.028
Motherfucker's lyin'.

43:53.064 --> 43:54.134
Rust.

43:56.234 --> 43:58.339
- It's good to see you.
- Bullshit.

44:05.943 --> 44:08.150
I talked to Marty.

44:08.246 --> 44:10.692
Well, you talked to the cops, too.

44:10.781 --> 44:12.283
Yes, them, too.

44:13.584 --> 44:15.461
How are you?

44:15.520 --> 44:17.522
What did Many tell you?

44:17.622 --> 44:19.966
He wanted to know
what the police asked me about.

44:20.024 --> 44:23.437
He said he was helpin' you with somethin'.
That's it.

44:25.296 --> 44:28.470
- How long you've been back?
- Hear you got a big house.

44:29.033 --> 44:31.980
Marty says the girls are doin' fine.

44:32.036 --> 44:33.037
That's good.

44:34.839 --> 44:39.379
Rust, just tell me it's somethin'
that's not gonna get him hurt.

44:40.711 --> 44:42.850
Well, I can! tell you that.

44:45.616 --> 44:49.564
It never sat right with me then,
and it doesn't now.

44:49.654 --> 44:52.294
You askin' me to lie to you about him.

44:54.158 --> 44:57.332
Get on out of here.
You're classin' the place up.

45:05.703 --> 45:07.683
Why did you quit, Marty?

45:08.673 --> 45:11.347
What's the real reason? What happened?

45:11.409 --> 45:14.253
You tell me why you come back, for real.

45:14.345 --> 45:15.688
Mmm, you first.

45:17.381 --> 45:18.917
Why'?! You quit?

45:19.817 --> 45:23.390
Well, I saw somethin'.

45:24.655 --> 45:25.861
A baby.

45:28.593 --> 45:32.769
Tweaker tried to
dry the kid in a microwave.

45:42.573 --> 45:45.349
Saw that, what he'd done, and I thought,

45:48.446 --> 45:49.948
"Never again."

45:52.016 --> 45:57.466
I thought I never wanted to look
at anything like that anymore.

46:00.358 --> 46:01.462
Ahem.

46:04.028 --> 46:05.371
Your turn.

46:06.264 --> 46:09.370
Why'd you, uh... Why'd you come back?

46:15.706 --> 46:16.980
For this.

46:18.075 --> 46:20.112
Somelhin' I had to see to.

46:21.779 --> 46:24.419
Before getting on with somethin' else.

46:31.922 --> 46:36.496
My life's been a circle
of violence and degradation

46:36.594 --> 46:38.505
long as I can remember.

46:40.431 --> 46:42.411
I'm ready to tie it off.

46:45.569 --> 46:47.310
See you on the boat.

47:00.584 --> 47:05.795
After the other day, I was thinkin',
"Why don't I see Steve and the boys more?"

47:07.191 --> 47:09.762
Ain't been out to my camp in a while.

47:11.429 --> 47:16.105
You know, if I don't get out here
three or four times a year,

47:16.500 --> 47:19.606
- I'm a basket case.
- I hear you.

47:22.173 --> 47:23.652
Ah.

47:24.141 --> 47:27.850
I do love a reason to drink beer
first thing in the mornin'.

47:30.448 --> 47:31.950
Oh.

47:32.183 --> 47:35.130
- Say, Steve, I was wanting to ask...
- Mmm'?

47:36.654 --> 47:40.796
You know that Fontenot girl,
remember, goin' off with her daddy?

47:42.193 --> 47:43.672
I just wasn't clear.

47:43.728 --> 47:48.040
Was it you knew for a fact
that she went with her daddy?

47:48.132 --> 47:50.908
Or somebody told you that's what happened?

47:52.203 --> 47:55.377
The family talked to Sheriff Childress.

47:55.473 --> 47:59.011
The girl's aunt and uncle, he knew them.

48:00.144 --> 48:01.316
Mmm-hmm.

48:03.547 --> 48:05.049
Who were they?

48:11.055 --> 48:15.197
I'm staﬂin' to think this wasn't just
a friendly invitation from an old pal, huh?

48:15.259 --> 48:17.068
It's definitely that.

48:18.162 --> 48:19.903
Well, then try this, then.

48:19.997 --> 48:22.273
I said all I remember about the girl,

48:22.366 --> 48:25.711
let's just have a good time
and don't ask again.

48:26.904 --> 48:30.943
- I'm with you 150% on that.
- All right.

48:31.842 --> 48:33.515
Thing is, Steve,

48:35.179 --> 48:36.351
I ain't gonna ask you.

48:39.450 --> 48:40.690
He is.

48:46.090 --> 48:48.400
I wouldn't if I was you, Steve.

48:50.528 --> 48:53.031
You're out of your jurisdiction,
Sheriff.

48:53.097 --> 48:56.237
You realize who I am now, you assholes?

48:56.300 --> 48:58.871
Yeah, I wouldn't be here if I didn't.

49:00.371 --> 49:01.975
- Marty...
- Don't look at me.

49:02.072 --> 49:04.609
I ain't never been able to control him.

49:04.708 --> 49:05.709
Come on.

49:06.744 --> 49:08.724
You're done after this.

49:08.779 --> 49:11.623
I'll have boss cracker
spliﬂin' your ass in Angola.

49:11.715 --> 49:13.115
Yeah, we'll talk about that,

49:14.151 --> 49:16.062
and some other things. Come on.

49:33.404 --> 49:36.681
That church Cohle talked about,
supposed to be right here.

49:36.774 --> 49:39.254
- We're lost.
- We're not lost.

49:39.310 --> 49:41.483
We goin' in the right direction,
we're headin' south.

49:41.579 --> 49:43.149
And that's gonna head us to 49.

49:43.247 --> 49:45.750
No, we're not looking for the 49.
We're lookin' for the church.

49:45.816 --> 49:48.319
I know we're looking for the church,
we ain't got to no church.

49:48.419 --> 49:50.160
Ain't seen nothing that
even resemble no church.

49:50.254 --> 49:51.494
Ain't nobody out here to even ask.

49:51.589 --> 49:54.331
Just let me know when you see somethin'.
Let me know when you see somethin'.

49:54.425 --> 49:55.927
There ain't nothin' to see.

50:00.364 --> 50:02.105
Hey! Hey!

50:06.437 --> 50:07.438
YES, sir.

50:07.505 --> 50:11.715
You know there's a little church around
here? Pretty old'? Black minister?

50:11.809 --> 50:14.119
You must mean Son of Life, sir.

50:15.279 --> 50:17.623
That place shut down.

50:17.681 --> 50:20.321
'05 I think. Just after
all them hurricanes.

50:20.618 --> 50:21.619
Mmm.

50:23.120 --> 50:26.693
- You live around here?
- No, sir. I live in St. Martin.

50:26.824 --> 50:28.360
Got a parish contract.

50:28.459 --> 50:31.963
Take care of some
cemeteries, public schools.

50:32.029 --> 50:34.134
All right. Thanks.

50:34.198 --> 50:37.805
- Hey. You know how to get to 49 from here?
- Sure.

50:37.868 --> 50:43.250
About a half mile, you'll see
a left, PR 1435, take that.

50:44.041 --> 50:48.990
About seven miles of fields,
you'll hit 49 before Crowley.

50:49.046 --> 50:51.720
- Know your way around, huh?
- Oh, yeah, boss.

50:51.815 --> 50:53.590
I know the whole coast.

50:53.684 --> 50:54.992
- My family...
- Thanks.

51:15.439 --> 51:19.216
My family's been here a long, long time.
